---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import HowItWorks from '../components/HowItWorks.astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import {chapters} from '../data/content.json';
const total=chapters.reduce((n,c)=>n+c.verses_count,0).toLocaleString('en-US');
---
<Shell title="Is It in the Quran?"><section class="intro"><div class="intro-top"><span class="pill mono-chip"><span class="dot"></span>{total} ayat</span></div> <h1>{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Search Arabic and Pickthall wording for any ayah or reference.</p><img class="motif" src="/motif.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="220" height="120" /></section><section class="panel"><form id="search-form" class="panel-body"><label class="field">Phrase or Quran reference<input id="query" type="search" placeholder="e.g. with hardship, or 94:5-6" maxlength="300" required autocomplete="off" dir="auto"/></label><div class="filters top-gap"><label class="field">Search text<select id="language"><option value="english">Pickthall · English</option><option value="arabic">Uthmani · Arabic (normalized)</option></select></label> <label class="field">Chapter<select id="chapter"><option value="0">All 114 chapters</option>{chapters.map(c=><option value={c.number}>{c.number}. {c.name_simple}</option>)}</select></label> <button class="button" id="submit">Search Quran</button></div> <div class="actions top-gap"><span class="micro">Try a search:</span> {['with hardship','every soul','94:5-6'].map(q=><><button type="button" class="pill" data-example={q}>{q}</button>{' '}</>)}</div><label class="check-label"><input id="remember" type="checkbox"/> Keep up to 5 recent searches in this browser for 30 days</label><div id="recent" class="actions top-gap"></div></form></section><aside class="sidebar"><HowItWorks><p>Search every ayah in Uthmani Arabic and Pickthall’s English translation. Start with a phrase or a reference.</p><p>Punctuation and case are ignored. Arabic diacritics, tatweel, and common alif variants are normalized. No stemming or semantic judgment is used.</p><p><strong>An empty wording search does not mean “not in the Quran.”</strong> Other translations and paraphrases may express an idea differently. Read the full context and consult qualified scholarship for interpretation.</p><p><a href="/claims/"><strong>Common claims</strong>: check twelve things people often say <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></HowItWorks></aside><section id="results" class="top-gap" aria-live="polite"><div class="empty"><h2>What would you like to check?</h2><p>The local text loads when you run your first search.</p><p><a href="/claims/">Common claims: check twelve things people often say <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></section><noscript><p class="noscript">Local searching requires JavaScript. You can read the source editions through the Sources page.</p></noscript><script>import '../lib/app';</script></Shell>
<style>.intro{position:relative}.intro .motif{position:absolute;right:0;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--accent);opacity:.55;pointer-events:none}@media(max-width:580px){.intro .motif{display:none}}.verse-context{margin-top:12px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}.verse-context summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center}.verse-context p{margin:6px 0;line-height:1.6}.verse-context .ctx-ref{font-size:.72rem}</style>
